From: j7 console
Subject: a5xelte fbcon: stop the panel console, whichever console op draws it

The boot log keeps running into the panel after the GUI starts.  0328 gated _cnputc only when
cons_ops_index was VC_CONS_OPS, but this board has no Apple video console: cons_ops_index stays on
SERIAL_CONS_OPS and serial_putc_options falls back to fbcon_putc(), which is what paints the panel,
so the gate never fired.  Mute every console op once the GUI has presented; _cnputs() has already
appended the line to the persistent eMMC log by then, and a panic or the debugger still draws.

diff --git a/osfmk/console/serial_console.c b/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
index cd63f3f..f30582b 100644
--- a/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
+++ b/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
@@ -250,11 +250,11 @@ _cnputc(char c, bool poll)
 
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_A5XELTE)
 	extern int sweet_console_muted;
-	/* The video console paints through cons_ops[] from here, not only through _cnputs() (which
-	 * drains the ring): without this the panel keeps showing log text after a5fb_noconsole=1.
-	 * _cnputs() appends to the persistent log before it reaches this function, so the log keeps
-	 * everything; a panic and the debugger still draw. */
-	if (idx == VC_CONS_OPS && sweet_console_muted && !panic_active() && !in_debugger) {
+	/* Every console op paints here, not only the video one: this board keeps cons_ops_index on
+	 * SERIAL_CONS_OPS and serial_putc_options falls back to fbcon_putc(), which is what draws the
+	 * panel.  _cnputs() has already appended the line to the persistent log before this runs, so
+	 * the log keeps everything; a panic and the debugger still draw. */
+	if (sweet_console_muted && !panic_active() && !in_debugger) {
 		return;
 	}
 #endif
